Execute a command in an authorized directory with cwd and .cronrc environment

Usage:
  cron-person exec <dir> [--] <command...> [flags]

Arguments:
  <dir>               Target directory path
  <command...>        Shell command to execute in directory

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for exec

Global Flags:
      --config string   Path to custom configuration file (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cron-person/config.json)
      --store string    Path to custom authorization state file (default: $XDG_STATE_HOME/cron-person/allowed.json)
